# TestingBot credentials — TEMPLATE. Copy, do not edit this file.
#
#   cp apps/bench-web/.env.testingbot.example apps/bench-web/.env.testingbot
#
# Then put your real key and secret in the COPY. Find them on the TestingBot
# dashboard under Account > API Key.
#
# The copy is git-ignored (.gitignore: `apps/*/.env.testingbot`), this template
# is not — that split is deliberate, so the template ships and the secrets never
# do. This repository becomes public at the OSS launch, so a committed
# credential here would be an incident, not an inconvenience. Do not rename the
# copy to anything else: the ignore rule matches `.env.testingbot` exactly.
#
# Usage — Node loads it explicitly, nothing loads it implicitly:
#
#   node --env-file=apps/bench-web/.env.testingbot apps/bench-web/scripts/testingbot-probe.mjs
#
# Or, without a file at all, for a one-off in PowerShell:
#
#   $env:TESTINGBOT_KEY="..."
#   $env:TESTINGBOT_SECRET="..."
#   node apps/bench-web/scripts/testingbot-probe.mjs
#
# The probe reads these two variables from the environment for the lifetime of
# one process. It never prints, logs, writes, or caches them.

TESTINGBOT_KEY=your-testingbot-key-here
TESTINGBOT_SECRET=your-testingbot-secret-here
